Description: Floating windows: snap to edges and corners, easier resize grab
 Windows-style window management for sway's floating windows, built into
 the compositor because sway's IPC reports no pointer position and no drag
 start or end, so no outside program can do it properly.
 .
 Snapping: drag a floating window (by its title bar, or with the floating
 modifier) to a screen edge or corner. A translucent preview in the theme's
 indicator colour shows where it will land; release to snap it to that
 half, quarter, or (top edge) the whole workspace. Bars and gaps are left
 clear. Dragging a snapped window away gives it back its old size.
 .
 Resize grab: floating windows get an invisible band around them that
 starts a resize, and the stretch of border near a corner counts as the
 corner. Without it the only grab area is the border itself.
 .
 New commands:
   floating_snap enable|disable     drag-to-edge snapping (default: enable)
   floating_grab_margin <px>        the resize band, 0-64 (default: 8)
   snap left|right|max|top-left|top-right|bottom-left|bottom-right|restore
                                    snap the focused floating window
 Both settings default to on, so Tebian's config needs no lines that an
 unpatched sway would reject. Most code is in new files (tree/snap.c,
 commands/snap.c); the hooks in existing files are small, to keep the
 patch easy to carry to new releases.
 .
 Applies to SwayFX 0.6.
Author: Tebian <https://github.com/tebian-os/tebian>
